+# Current repair: 0ab5dc1f5386 v4.1.1
+
+The retained v4.1.0 lesson at seed 4, indices 1..5, medium has four demonstrations
+that fit both row-major and column-first source selection, then a query differing
+in five cells. All five intended labels were executed through protected Racket.
+The exact old-source witness is `counterexamples/column-order-lesson.json`.
+
+Version 4.1.1 reserves NE/SW quadrants for the two competing scan-order sources;
+row and column priorities therefore disagree under every allowed jitter. Other
+profiles keep the original placement procedure. The declared `column_first`
+rival uses the same crop-value one-use semantics; the actual worker now rejects
+the retained old lesson instead of passing it. Canonical Racket/authority and
+rule hash `1529a4ef373b` are unchanged; no audit-resolution record was edited.
+
+Six new regressions were first red and then green. The full task-local staged
+suite passes 50 tests. A separate protected-Racket replay checked 16 inputs:
+one four-demo/four-query repaired lesson and eight boundary-band witnesses.
+The new tests also cover 96 scan-order layouts and 16 rotated lesson windows.
+These are finite checks, not a full peer battery or owner acceptance. The owner
+should replay the exact source and resolve the inherited column-order audit only
+after integration; no approval hashes were changed.
+
+Current generator SHA-256: `adee300add5f0b4c7d3ba8b3f329ab9a86f32a9f371a091aed41cc4240dfd8bd`.
+
+## Imported historical notes (measurements below predate v4.1.1)
